<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fu Youde</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1394</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fu Youde was a general of the founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Hongwu Emperor</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a>. In 1371 he led one of the armies that conquered the Ming Xia state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a>, and in the following years he campaigned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> in the north. In 1381 he commanded the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a> from the last Yuan loyalists. Ennobled as Duke of Ying, he was forced to commit suicide in 1394 during the emperor's purges.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fu-youde.jpg" alt="Fu Youde" width="320" height="583" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous (Category:Ming dynasty)Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ming_Dynasty_Portrait_of_Fu_Youde.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
